// Suppression list for `npm run audit` (audit-ci wraps `npm audit`).
//
// Every entry below is a current finding that has been reviewed and accepted
// in writing. New advisories that appear later will surface as a fresh failure
// instead of being silently swallowed — that is the whole point of using
// audit-ci over `npm audit` (which has no native suppression mechanism).
//
// When upgrading a flagged dependency, REMOVE its entry from `allowlist` so
// audit-ci confirms the fix instead of permanently masking it.
{
  // Fail the command on anything moderate or higher.
  "moderate": true,

  "allowlist": [
    // ── xlsx (SheetJS) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // Used WRITE-ONLY in this repo to generate downloadable .xlsx exports
    // (src/utils/export/exportPnLComparison.ts, exportBWBComparison.ts).
    // Both CVEs require *parsing* attacker-controlled .xlsx input via
    // XLSX.read / XLSX.readFile, code paths we never call. The ToS
    // paperMoney CSV upload uses a hand-rolled parser at
    // api/_lib/csv-parser/parse.ts and does not touch xlsx.
    // No npm fix exists; SheetJS publishes patches at cdn.sheetjs.com only.
    "GHSA-4r6h-8v6p-xvw6", // Prototype Pollution in SheetJS
    "GHSA-5pgg-2g8v-p4x9", // SheetJS ReDoS

    // ── @vercel/node transitive deps ──────────────────────────────────────
    // @vercel/node is a devDependency used by `vercel dev` / `vercel build`
    // locally. Vercel's production runtime ships its own bundled toolchain,
    // so none of these CVEs are reachable from deployed code.
    // `npm audit fix --force` would downgrade @vercel/node 5.x → 3.0.1,
    // which is the wrong direction (loses Fluid Compute / Node 24 support).

    "GHSA-2g4f-4pwh-qvx6", // ajv ReDoS via $data — build-time JSON schema only
    "GHSA-9wv6-86v2-598j", // path-to-regexp backtracking — build-time routing

    // undici is NOT allowlisted: package.json `overrides` forces undici onto
    // the patched 6.x line (`^6.29.1`) under both of its 6.x users. Nested
    // overrides only apply inside the named package, so each needs an entry.
    // - @vercel/node: every release through 27.0.2 (checked 2026-10-23)
    //   hard-pins undici 5.28.4, and the 5.x line has no fix for the
    //   6.24–6.29.0 advisories, so no parent upgrade exists. It only calls
    //   undici's `request` and `Headers` (in its `vercel dev` server), both
    //   stable across 5→6.
    // - @vercel/blob: a production runtime dependency (backup/archive crons,
    //   api/ml plots, Periscope and Take-It bundle storage) whose own
    //   `^6.23.0` range (through 2.8.2) still admits 6.23–6.29.0.
    // Remove each entry once `npm view <pkg> dependencies.undici` reports
    // >=6.29.1.

    // zod is NOT allowlisted: package.json `overrides` forces
    // @vercel/cli-config's zod onto `^4.6.6` (GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5). Every
    // @vercel/cli-config release through 0.3.3 (checked 2026-10-23)
    // exact-pins zod 4.1.11, so no parent upgrade fixes it. The override
    // only lands on cli-config <=0.2.5 (today 0.2.0, via @vercel/functions
    // 3.6.2 → @vercel/oidc 3.6.0), whose dist/index.js re-exports modules
    // that require("zod"). cli-config >=0.2.6 (pulled by @vercel/functions
    // >=3.9.7) inlines zod 4.1.11 into dist/index.js, where no override can
    // reach it and npm audit cannot see it, so do not bump
    // @vercel/functions past 3.9.6 (.github/dependabot.yml ignores >=3.9.7).
    // Reachability: the @vercel/functions package root never loads
    // @vercel/oidc (only the `@vercel/functions/oidc` subpath does), this
    // repo imports only `waitUntil` from the root, and cli-config's zod
    // only parses local Vercel CLI auth/config files. Once
    // `npm view @vercel/cli-config dependencies.zod` reports >=4.6.6, drop
    // the override and the Dependabot ignore.

    // glob is NOT allowlisted: package.json `overrides` forces glob onto
    // the patched 14.x line (`^14.0.2`, GHSA-3g3m-2fjr-6pw4: an aborted
    // async walk keeps reading directories) under each of its three users.
    // Nested overrides only apply inside the named package, so each needs
    // an entry. No parent upgrade exists (checked 2026-11-03): the latest
    // @sentry/bundler-plugin-core 5.3.0 (and @sentry/bundler-plugins 11.10.0
    // behind @sentry/vite-plugin 11.x) and @vercel/nft 1.11.0 depend on
    // `glob ^13`, and workbox-build 7.4.1 (the latest) on `glob ^11`.
    // The jump is safe for all three. glob 14 removes the `debug` option,
    // renames Pattern/Processor internals, makes walk() return arrays and
    // roots an `ignore` pattern that starts with `/` at the cwd root. Each
    // parent calls only glob()/globSync() with cwd, absolute, nodir,
    // ignore, dot, mark and follow, and none passes `signal`. For those
    // call shapes glob 11.1.0, 13.0.6 and 14.0.3 return identical file sets
    // on this repo's dist/ and on a tree with node_modules and dot
    // directories. All three are build-time tools: the Sentry plugin and
    // workbox-build run in `vite build`, nft inside @vercel/node. glob 14
    // also depends on minimatch ^11.0.2, which clears GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249
    // on these three paths. Remove each entry once
    // `npm view <parent> dependencies.glob` reports >=14.0.2.

    // ── minimatch (dev and build tooling only) ────────────────────────────
    // GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249: at `optimizationLevel >= 2` a crafted glob
    // pattern amplifies minimatch's internal pattern list
    // (firstPhasePreProcess), then a quadratic pass (secondPhasePreProcess)
    // exhausts CPU and memory. Fixed in 11.0.1. After the glob overrides
    // above, three copies below 11.0.1 remain (checked 2026-11-03):
    // - 10.2.6 at the root: eslint, @eslint/config-array,
    //   @typescript-eslint/typescript-estree, eslint-plugin-import-x and
    //   eslint-plugin-sonarjs, i.e. the lint chain.
    // - 3.1.5 under @ts-morph/common (ts-morph 12, pinned by @vercel/node
    //   and @vercel/static-config): `vercel dev` / `vercel build` only.
    // - 5.1.9 under filelist (jake, ejs, workbox-build's off-main-thread
    //   plugin): never loaded, since ejs's lib does not require jake.
    //
    // No fix exists:
    // - Parent upgrade: the latest eslint 10.14.0, eslint-plugin-sonarjs
    //   4.2.2, typescript-estree 8.72.1, @eslint/config-array 0.23.5,
    //   eslint-plugin-import-x 4.17.1 and @ts-morph/common 0.29.0 all still
    //   depend on `minimatch ^10` (import-x: `^9 || ^10`), and @vercel/node
    //   29.0.1 still pins ts-morph 12.0.0.
    // - Override: unsafe. minimatch 11 drops makeRe(), and import-x's ESM
    //   entry does `import { makeRe } from 'minimatch'`
    //   (rules/no-internal-modules.js), a SyntaxError at load, so the root
    //   copy must stay on 10.x. @ts-morph/common and filelist call
    //   `require('minimatch')` as a function, which is an object in 11
    //   (TypeError). Moving only eslint, config-array, typescript-estree
    //   and sonarjs to 11 would not remove this entry, and would run every
    //   lint on a major eslint has not adopted: its file walk calls
    //   Minimatch#match(path, partial), whose `**` handling 11 changes.
    //
    // Reachability: the vulnerable code runs only when `optimizationLevel`
    // is 2 or more, and the default is 1. None of the lint packages sets
    // it (grepped in node_modules). The one level-2 caller in the tree is
    // glob, which now resolves minimatch 11.0.4. 3.1.5 and 5.1.9 predate
    // the code: they have no firstPhasePreProcess, secondPhasePreProcess or
    // optimizationLevel. The patterns are this repo's own lint globs, rule
    // options and dependency names, never request input, and nothing here
    // ships to production. Remove this entry once `npm ls minimatch` shows
    // no copy below 11.0.1.
    "GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249", // minimatch globparts amplification
  ],
}
